1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,322
I remember when these fields were green...

2
00:00:03,583 --> 00:00:05,279
Before the droughts started.

3
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:08,191
As trapped greenhouse
gases warmed the planet,

4
00:00:08,191 --> 00:00:12,553
heatwaves lasted longer and evaporated
water right out of the soil.

5
00:00:12,813 --> 00:00:16,443
NASA’s SMAP satellite watched Earth's
soil moisture drop from space—

6
00:00:16,443 --> 00:00:20,200
showing how farms across the
world were drying out into dust.

7
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:21,961
Then came the smoke.

8
00:00:22,435 --> 00:00:24,935
Every summer, dried-out
forests caught fire

9
00:00:24,935 --> 00:00:27,876
easier and burned hotter than ever before.

10
00:00:28,350 --> 00:00:32,113
Tiny smoke particles—called aerosols—
floated high into the sky,

11
00:00:32,113 --> 00:00:35,200
blocking the sunlight
plants needed to grow.

12
00:00:37,600 --> 00:00:41,741
Firestorms grew so huge they created
their own weather—blasting smoke past

13
00:00:41,741 --> 00:00:46,327
the rain clouds into the stratosphere,
where it stayed trapped for years.

14
00:00:46,927 --> 00:00:50,579
NASA’s FIRMS fire maps lit up
red across every continent...

15
00:00:51,179 --> 00:00:54,717
We watched the warning signs,
until there was nowhere left to run.

